  triage:description "arch-ctm's M5 investigation found the admission-capacity runner reports a daemon cleanup/shutdown failure at the 10-second mark even though the daemon process actually exits shortly afterward — the shutdown evidence recorded by the runner is inaccurate (false-negative cleanup failure), which risks masking real readiness/leak issues in future runs and needs correction. FOLLOWUP: arch-ctm confirms fix in commits 1b0f8ab8/4100afee — cleanup_failure=null in latest M5 evidence, no daemon leak." ;
